      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>So I rather like Love Letter, but I&#39;m not that keen on the original art and I absolutely detest the remake art. I don&#39;t think I could stand to look at either one for very long.</p><p>And I love Sentinels, and I have a Love Letter-sized hole in the Printer&#39;s Studio order I&#39;m putting together to take advantage of the current coupon...</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So what I need to work out is, which character for which role? And what&#39;s the theme? Of course in regular LL you&#39;re trying to get enough letters to the princess that she falls in love with you, but that wouldn&#39;t work here. Any thoughts/suggestions/random abuse?</p><p><strong>5 x Guard&nbsp;</strong>(1)&nbsp;- guess another player&#39;s hand, if you&#39;re right they are out of the round. 5 different characters here would be fun.</p><p><strong>2 x Priest&nbsp;</strong>(2) - look at another player&#39;s hand. Visionary and, er, someone else who could maybe predict stuff in some way, maybe?</p><p><strong>2 x Baron&nbsp;</strong>(3) - compare hands with another player, player with lower card is out of the round.</p><p><strong>2 x Handmaiden&nbsp;</strong>(4) - immunity to effects. I&#39;m thinking Legacy (Lead from the Front) and Wraith (Smoke Bombs)?</p><p><strong>2 x Prince&nbsp;</strong>(5) - one player (can target self) discards hand and draws a new card. Perhaps Fanatic (End of Days) and Parse (Buffer Overflow)?</p><p><strong>1 x King&nbsp;</strong>(6) - swap hands with another player.</p><p><strong>1 x Countess&nbsp;</strong>(7) - must discard if in hand with King or Prince.</p><p><strong>1 x Princess&nbsp;</strong>(8) - if discarded, player is out of the round.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Disclaimer: this will be for personal use only, and the Love Letter guys are okay with rethemes as long as they aren&#39;t shared. Nothing stopping anyone else making their own version though, right? To support the publishers I&#39;ll buy a copy of the game and give it away as a gift so I don&#39;t have to look at it. Man, that art is fugly.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
